# Line-endings policy (see agents/plan/PROGRESS.md errata, 2026-11-15;
# agents/notes/pitfalls/expect-test-eol.md).
#
# The repo stores text as LF. A `core.autocrlf=true` checkout (the default on
# many Windows setups) rewrote fixture files to CRLF, which broke the
# byte-exact `expect!` CST snapshots in crates/oxidizr-dsl/tests/m1_lossless.rs.
# `.gitattributes` has priority over core.autocrlf, so these rules make every
# checkout byte-stable on all three CI OSes.

# Text files: normalize to LF in the repo, check out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The test corpus is a byte contract: vendored .dsl fixtures, golden .json
# workspaces, docs and assets must survive checkout verbatim (no EOL
# conversion in either direction — re-vendoring must keep reference bytes).
testdata/** -text

# Binaries (belt-and-braces beyond heuristic detection).
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.gif -text
*.ico -text
*.jar -text
*.pdf -text
*.zip -text
